        // r2-pancerz (PLAN 1.7, Jeff 09.10 "ladry wedlug Jazdy"): ladry u bohaterow wedlug Jazdy - jak na ekranie gry (ROT ExtraGearRequirements) i u zolnierzy
        public bool HeroBardingNeedsRiding = true;         // horse barding and saddles ask Riding of you, your companions and the lords too - the same rule as for soldiers. Realm of Thrones' own gear requirements (on by default) already make the inventory screen refuse barding above your Riding; this makes the rest follow the screen: Spoils' auto-equip of companions, your starting kit, a lord taking renowned barding by the custom of war (what he cannot ride with goes to his baggage). With Realm of Thrones' requirements off, the screen refuses barding above your Riding by this rule. What anyone already wears stays on him. Off = barding is not checked for heroes, except by the game's own screen
        public bool HeroSkillToOwnGear = false;            // AI lords, companions and your grown family get the Athletics, Bow and Crossbow their own battle gear demands (armour, arrows, bolts) - raised, never lowered - so that nobody loses his armour to Hero Gear Requirements: on load, whenever the game dresses a hero from a template, and in a daily check. Works only while Hero Gear Requirements is on. You are never raised. Raised skills open their perks too: the game picks them for AI lords (Imposing Stature and Merry Men give a commander 5 more men), your companions and family get them as perk picks. Applied by CrashScribe; turning it off does not lower skills already raised
        public int WeaponSkillPerTier = 35;                // Weapon Tier Law: a weapon or shield needs at least (tier - 1) x this in its skill, whatever the data says - a tier 6 blade wants 175, so a One Handed 30 bandit never 'qualifies' for it; 0 turns the law off. Applied at session start

