        public bool BeatenPurseToVictor = true;            // the victors take the whole purse of a beaten caravan, village cart party or bandit band that has no hero at its head - you, the lords and the bandits alike (until now the game gave the victors only a tenth of a caravan's or villagers' coin and half of a band's, and the rest vanished with the beaten party). The purse is shared among the victors by their part in the battle, just as the game shares its plunder; what no victor can carry (a militia, a patrol, the Others) stays in the beaten purse and, once the beaten party is gone, goes to the party that beat it, else to the coffers of that party's town, castle or village, else of the nearest town (a village cart party's purse goes on by Villager Purse Survives). With Crown Thirds, a realm at war takes a ninth of what its lords - and you, as a vassal - take this way, and of the coin a caravan or village cart party hands you without a fight (it surrenders, you take it captive, or it pays you to let it pass). A party that was not beaten in battle - a band that joins you, a party wiped out on the winning side - keeps the old rule: its purse vanishes with it. Off = the game's tenth and half, the rest vanishes as before
