        // BattlefieldLaw: LootTag, QueueWreck, AfterDtePartyItems, AfterGenerateLoot; LootTally.FelledPost)
        public bool LootStateFromWounds = true;            // armour stripped from a foe your party brought down comes in the state the blows left it in: every hit of this battle wears the piece it struck exactly as your own armour wears, from the state it had before the battle (480 points off a 2000-point mail shirt leaves 76% - Damaged). The piece smashed by the killing blow and the piece Dynamic Troop Equipment counts as broken are judged the same way: only a true wreck comes to you whole; a better piece is shared like the rest of that foe's gear (yours whole if you or a companion felled him, the captain's share if your men did - the rest to the army armoury). Gear battered to Loot Min Condition Percent or less is destroyed. Needs Gear Four States. Off: as before
        // m114-lup (Jeff 24.10 17:40: "ja wszystkich sam zabijam, to wszystko powinno byc moje"; regula stanu m110 - stan z rzeczywistosci, nie z loterii):
