        public bool DuelistsInBattles = true;              // in battles (the field, siege assaults and defences, sallies, raids) and hideouts lords, companions and other heroes fight like the duellists of the lists: from about skill 100 (on Realistic) a hero attacks on his own, ripostes after a parry, feints and kicks, and does not wait behind his guard - the higher his best weapon skill, the bolder, and with Veterans By Tier never weaker than a veteran of his tier; soldiers keep the veterans' rule. Needs RBM with posture. Off = heroes fight as soldiers of their tier (level, or skill with Hero Tier From Skill), as before
        public bool HeroTierFromSkill = true;              // with Veterans By Tier: in battles and hideouts a hero counts as a soldier of the tier his best weapon skill earns when that is higher than his level's tier: best skill 40 = tier I, every 30 points a tier more (100 = III, 160 = V, 190 = VI, 220 and more = VII). It matters most with Duelists In Battles off; with it on, it covers heroes below the duellist profile (best skill under about 125 on Realistic, more on Hard and Easy) and the least a duellist hero keeps. Off = tier from level only, as before
        public bool VeteranAggressionFix = true;           // with Veterans By Tier: veterans (tier IV and up) no longer break their attacks off more often than plain RBM - before, their experience also made them give up attacks more readily, which made them more passive, not less. How readily a soldier starts an attack still follows his tier (recruits hesitate, veterans press on), and tiers I-III keep the old rule. Off = both chances scaled for every tier, as before
        public bool DuelSkillGapInBattles = true;          // in battles and hideouts the Duel Skill Gap Weight rule also counts in your own clashes (when you strike or are struck), the same rule both ways as in the lists: the better fighter's guard suffers less from blocked or parried blows and the weaker one's more (limits 0.75x-1.25x, as soldiers' guards already grow with their tier). Clashes between other fighters are untouched. Off = plain RBM in battles, as before
        public bool DuelistBurstsInBattles = true;         // with Duelists In Battles: a skilled hero in a battle or hideout seizes his moment as in the lists - when an attacker's guard breaks on him he strikes back at once (about a second, then at least 2 seconds before the next), and when he is kept on the defence he answers with a flurry of his own (from skill 140, then at least 6 seconds' rest). Heroes only. Off = steady behaviour

