        public bool RansomRepeatCheaper = true;            // with Lord Ransom By Income: a lord or lady ransomed again within Ransom Repeat Days of their last ransom costs less - Ransom Repeat Floor of the price right after the last ransom, rising evenly to the full price after Ransom Repeat Days. The family has just paid once, and the captor takes what it can still raise. The same for every way of ransoming (between AI houses, by courier, through a broker, from your party screen) and for a king paid by his treasury; your own ransom when you are a captive is unchanged. The coin still goes from the captive's family to the captor - only less of it. Off = every ransom at the full price, as before
        public int RansomRepeatDays = 56;                  // with Ransom Repeat Cheaper: for how many days after a ransom the next ransom of the same person is cheaper (56 = eight weeks)
        public float RansomRepeatFloor = 0.25f;            // with Ransom Repeat Cheaper: the share of the full price a ransom costs right after the last one (0.25 = a quarter); it rises evenly to the full price over Ransom Repeat Days
