        public bool VassalRansomAid = true;                // with Lord Ransom By Income: when the head of an AI house or an AI king is ransomed and the family (for a king - the treasury) cannot pay all of it in coin, the realm's other landed houses chip in - each gives its share by its fiefs (a town counts as two castles), but never more than Vassal Ransom Aid Share of what its family holds above its reserve. Their coin goes with the rest of the cash to whoever is owed the ransom (the captor, or you when you sell the captive to a ransom broker), and the ransom debt is that much smaller. Your house is never asked, and a house in debt to the bank or below its reserve gives nothing. Off = the family pays alone, the rest is a debt as before
