        public bool FolkCirculationGuard = true;           // with Folk Hoard Tax: a steward of the realm's coin watches each day how much all the common folk - townsfolk, castle folk and villagers - hold against their normal level of savings. While they hold more than Folk Guard Band High times it, the hoard tax rises a little each day (up to Folk Guard Max Times the usual rate); while they hold less than Folk Guard Band Low times it, it falls a little each day (down to a quarter). It never takes more in a day than about one part in seven hundred of all the coin in the world, or twice what flows into the people's purses in a day, whichever is more, so an old hoard comes back slowly. Folk Guard Crown Share of every hoard tax goes to the treasury of the realm the place belongs to. Off = the hoard tax stays at Folk Hoard Tax Rate and goes only to the lord and the purse, as before
        public float FolkGuardBandLow = 1.25f;             // with Folk Circulation Guard: below this many times their normal level of savings the common folk pay less hoard tax each day
        public float FolkGuardBandHigh = 1.75f;            // with Folk Circulation Guard: above this many times their normal level of savings the common folk pay more hoard tax each day
