        public bool FolkGuardCrownToReserve = true;        // with Folk Circulation Guard: the treasury's part of the hoard tax is laid by in the treasury's reserve instead of being spent with the day's income - the crown pays it out slowly, like the rest of its reserve, instead of handing it to the houses the same day. Off = the treasury's part is spent with the day's income, as before
        public bool CrownTownLoans = true;                 // the crowns borrow from their towns: a realm at war whose treasury has fallen below its reserve for war (60 days of the wages it pays back to its houses, at least 500000) borrows what it lacks from the towns of the realm - at most half of what a town's purse holds above the merchants' stock and of what its labourers, craftsmen and merchant families hold above their normal savings, the richest first (not besieged towns, not your towns). The borrowed coin is kept in the treasury, not handed out. The towns earn Crown Town Loan Rate Year a year on it. In war the crown pays only the interest; in peace it repays the debt within about half a year, and it pays back early whenever its treasury is above its reserve for war. A crown that cannot pay in peace for Crown Town Loan Default Days days running defaults: the rest is lost to the towns, every town that lent loses 10 loyalty and the crown may not borrow from its towns for half a year. Off = the crowns do not borrow from their towns, as before (a debt already owed waits in the save)
