        public bool DailyLifeEstates = true;               // with Daily Life Measure: the estates of every town and village - slaves, peasants, labourers, craftsmen, merchants, gentry - are kept in the land's book and in the save (an old save gets them at the first dawn from the land's customs and its Banner Kings classes), and you can see them: the map tooltips of towns, castles (their region), villages and the villages of a district show the estates and their Livelihood, 'Estates and livelihood' in village, town and castle menus lists every estate of the place with its Livelihood, income and daily table, 'Look over the district' shows the district's estates, and 'Realm ledger' in town and castle menus lists the realm, its regions and the whole world. On its own it only labels and shows - nothing in the economy changes; but Daily Life Mobility, Freedom, Prosperity Link and War Scar (group 'Daily life - rise, fall and war') work only with it and do change the game (off = the estates are reckoned afresh each day for the log only, as before, the book kept in the save stays untouched, and those four stop too)

