        public bool KsLedgerCurrentRecipes = true;         // with Start Calibration applied and Ks Real Recipes: the goods ledger in the log counts the town craftsmen's meat and ale against the recipes in force (by weight) - until now it remembered the game's old recipes and showed some 1,700 pieces a day of meat and ale 'from nothing' that were never made, so a real leak could hide in that noise (log only; off = as before)
        public bool KsHidesByTable = true;                 // with Start Calibration applied and Ks Real Recipes: a beast slaughtered in a town - by the hidden craftsmen or at a butcher's - gives as many raw hides as the one world table counts for the same beast slaughtered in a village: 1.6 hides for a cow, 0.6 for a hog, 0.4 for a sheep (8, 5 and 10 kg of raw hide for each 100 kg of the beast). The fractions are tallied town by town and kept in the save; a whole hide reaches the stall each time a town's tally fills up. Until now a town sheep gave a whole hide (two and a half times a village sheep) and a butcher's cow five, and raw hides piled up unsold on every stall. Needs Artisan Own Inputs for the town craftsmen. Off = the recipes' round numbers, as before

