        // BEZ kalibracji KS (odstepstwo od projektu, galaz w-toku/noc-ds). Nowe klucze - nie ma ich w Armoury.json Jeffa (dzialaja domyslne). Wylaczenie DuesMedieval =
        // stare pobory wsi od nastepnej doby; zapis arm_daniny (zaleglosci, pierwsza doba DS, udzial korony przed wplywem dnia) zostaje bez skutku.
        // RECENZJA 17.10 (krytyczne): DuesMedieval DOMYSLNIE WYLACZONY - bez koszyka KS wies nie ma na co wydac uwolnionych pieniedzy (projekt rozdz. 3, 11, ryzyko 15.3;
        // model: kiesy wsi 4.5 -> 17.6 mln w 120 dob, korona -9.8% wplywu dnia, panowie -9.6% D stalego). Wlaczenie na zapisie Jeffa tylko jego decyzja, po autotescie 120 dob
        // z bramkami nds (NDS-3b, 3e, 7b, 7c, 9); odplyw bez towaru - roboty gminy (DsCommunalWorks).
        // WGRANIE 75 (17.10, Jeff: "Tak, wgraj" po tescie fin72 38/38): DuesMedieval DOMYSLNIE TAK (wsie F1; DsTowns dalej NIE, KS nie w tej galezi).
        public bool DuesMedieval = true;                  // the villages pay their lords and their king as they did in the Middle Ages: the lord's share, the tithe and - in war - the crown's share are taken from what the carts bring home, the moment they bring it, and a small fixed rent is paid first; nothing is taken any more as 'a share a day of whatever the village has saved' (the crown's war levy on village savings, the hoard tax, the lords' war levy from villages, the 5 percent Banner Kings village market). A village keeps three weeks of its needs and rent in its chest and spends on finer goods only what lies beyond it. The old takings fade out over Ds Ramp Days from the first day with this on (needs Town Folk Live; off by default until it is tested together with the village basket of the start calibration; off = the old rules from the next day)
        public bool DsVillageCartDues = true;              // with Dues Medieval: the tithe (Tithe Village Share of the takings, half of it back as alms for the village poor, half to build septs) and, in war, the crown's share are taken at the cart, from the village's part of the takings, the moment the cart comes home; the crown's share is also taken from what soldiers pay a village for lodging and services. Off = the tithe is taken from the village purse once a day as before and the crown takes no share from villages
        public float DsWarShareVillage = 0.10f;            // with Dues Medieval: the crown's share of the village's part of the takings (after the tithe) for each step of war grant - one step in war (one and a half with the War Tax policy), none in peace; 0.10 = a tenth in war, as the 'ninth' of sheaves, fleeces and lambs was granted to Edward III. Nothing is taken from a village that is raided or looted, whose town or castle is besieged, or whose people go hungry
        public bool DsRentArrears = true;                  // with Dues Medieval: the village's fixed rent (Village Dues Per Head Year) is paid first each day; what the purse cannot pay is written in the lord's book of arrears and paid first on the days after, instead of being lost. Off = unpaid rent is lost as before
        public int DsRentForgiveDays = 364;                // with Ds Rent Arrears: arrears older than this many days of rent are forgiven by the lord - the oldest debt goes first (0 = never forgiven)
        public bool DsRentRemitRaided = true;              // with Dues Medieval: on a day when the village's town or market town is besieged, or its people go hungry, the lord lets the day's rent go (a raided or looted village pays no rent anyway); the arrears wait. Off = the rent is due on those days too
        public int DsVillageChestDays = 21;                // with Dues Medieval: the village keeps this many days of its daily purchases and its rent in its chest for a black day - nothing beyond its daily needs and rent is spent below it, and the village lends to lords only from what lies above it
        public int DsSurplusSpendDays = 15;                // with Dues Medieval: a village spends each day one part in this many of what its purse holds beyond its chest on finer goods - half on the townsfolk's list of finer goods in its market town, half at its Banner Kings village market (0 = it spends nothing beyond its daily needs)
        public float DsSurplusBkShare = 0.5f;              // with Dues Medieval: the share of a village's spending beyond its chest that goes to its Banner Kings village market; the rest goes to the finer goods in its market town (without the Banner Kings village market - all of it)
        public int DsRampDays = 28;                        // with Dues Medieval: over how many days the old takings from village savings fade out and the crown's share at the cart and the spending beyond the chest come in, from the first day with Dues Medieval on - a running campaign (an old save) changes over step by step (0 = at once)
        public bool DsCommunalWorks = true;                // with Dues Medieval: what a village means to spend beyond its chest but finds no goods for on the shelves of its market town is spent on communal works - the church fabric, the mill, a bridge, the roads: three quarters as wages to the masons and carpenters of the market town, a quarter as material bought from its merchants (as the septs are built from the tithe). Off = what finds no goods stays in the village purse
        public int DsRentArrearsPayDays = 28;              // with Ds Rent Arrears: a village pays off its rent arrears at one part in this many a day (at least one day's rent), and only from what its purse holds beyond the day's needs - the arrears never take its bread (0 = all at once, as far as the purse goes)
        // m105-gospodarka4 G5 (21.10, n32: 34 nowe biedne wsie - utarg spadl, a czynsz placony pierwszy z calej kiesy): rata dnia czynszu tylko z kiesy ponad koszyk dnia
        // (ta sama zasada co zaleglosc; w dobie zakupu co 2. doby - koszyk 2 dob, TownFolk.VillageBuyDays), reszta do ksiegi zaleglosci. DsVillage.RentPay. Nowy klucz;
        // wylaczony = kod jak w WGRANIU 102. Progi: sprawdz_logi --grupa m105gosp4.
        public bool DsRentAfterBread = true;               // with Ds Rent Arrears: the village pays the day's fixed rent only from what its purse holds beyond the basket it buys that day (two days' basket on its market day with Ks Village Buy Every 2) - the rent never takes its bread, as the arrears already do; what it cannot pay goes into the lord's book of arrears (paid off later, forgiven after Ds Rent Forgive Days). Off = the day's rent is paid first from the whole purse, as before
        // m105-gospodarka5 (21.10, diagnoza gosp5: 73 z 569 wsi biednych w n32 - 64 Westeros; biedna wies placi ziarno i sol z oszczednosci, a pan bierze swoja dzialke
        // z wozu i czynsz z pieniedzy skrzyni): dopoki kiesa wsi DS jest ponizej skrzyni, pan oddaje wsi swoja dzialke z TEGO wozu (najwyzej do skrzyni; z licznika pana -
        // VillageTakings.LordRelief) i nie bierze czynszu z pieniedzy skrzyni (rata dnia tylko z kiesy ponad skrzynie, reszta darowana bez zaleglosci; rata zaleglosci
        // z kiesy ponad max(koszyk, skrzynia) - DsVillage.RentPay). Nowy klucz; wylaczony = kod jak w fd388555. Progi: sprawdz_logi --grupa m105gosp5.
        public bool DsLordReliefBelowChest = true;         // with Dues Medieval: while a village's purse holds less than its chest for a black day, its lord gives it back his share of what each cart brings home - only from that cart, and only as much as the chest still lacks - and takes the fixed rent only from what the purse holds beyond the chest (the rest of the day's rent is let go, not written as arrears; arrears are paid only from what lies beyond both the day's basket and the chest). The lord pays it from his current takings, never from his savings, and the relief stops by itself once the chest is full. Off = the lord takes his share at the cart and the rent as before

