        // go nie ma (dziala domyslna z kodu)
        public bool DsWarGrantTreasuryFirst = true;        // with Ds Towns: a king with a full treasury first pays for his war from his own treasure. What the treasury holds above its war reserve and above its debts to the Iron Bank and the towns pays the wage refunds and the war aid to the houses before the people are taxed (how it is spent - Ds War Grant Treasury To Reserve); while it does, the war grant may be nothing and the people pay no war aids, war tax on earnings or tenth that quarter (with the War Tax policy one step is still granted). Mercenary contracts, the Iron Bank's instalments, gifts, reparations and the price of allies called to war are paid from the day's income, so the people still grant what that income lacks for them (on a day the income falls short of them, see Ds War Grant Treasury Pays Dues). A grant changes by at most one step a quarter as before. When such a treasury falls to its war reserve, the realm grants a war grant the next day - unless the quarter day is no more than Ds Grant Session Days away, then on the quarter day. Off = the war grant follows the lack alone, as before
        // f23-korona (recenzja - odpowiedz 8a doslownie): TAK - nadanie 0, dopoki skarbiec jest ponad zapasem wojny i dlugami (skarbiec, ktory nie starczy na DsGrantSessionDays
        // braku, liczy sie jak bedacy przy zapasie - bez progu nadanie skakaloby 0 / krok co kwartal przy kilku zlotych nadwyzki); NIE - nadwyzka rozlozona na kwartal (1/91
