        public bool KsFarmSurplusCapNet = true;            // with Ks Farm Follows Surplus: a town's farm is raised for its merchants' surplus only up to what the merchants have really taken in over the last weeks (a year of their recent daily takings), by at most Ks Farm Surplus Review Max of the farm or of those takings, whichever is larger, at a time; the surplus is judged on the purse left after the coin it already owes, and nothing is measured or raised while the farms are still coming in after they were set. A town whose purse has fallen to one and a half times its working coin, or that owes part of its farm, has a farm above its merchants' takings lowered at the same pace (at most Ks Farm Surplus Review Max at a time, never below those takings). A town that pays no farm at all and keeps gathering coin gets a farm from its takings at that same pace, or pays the catch-up if it has no takings. The quarterly farm review of such a town never aims above its merchants' takings either. Off = raises up to Ks Farm Surplus Review Max of the farm whatever the takings, as before
        // m105-miasta G1 (21.10; log 102 Armoury-2026-10-21_14-29-20.log: NAKUM-27 12 -> 18 miast z KS ponizej zapasu kupcow, NKA-3 16 na koniec - obnizka z dochodu
